+---
+id: dl-003-validate-input-as-a-result-with-a-new-invalid-input-error-code
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate input as a Result, with a new invalid-input error code"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to `TaskList`, bypassing whatever validation a
+screen's own form might otherwise do, so an empty title, a 500-character title, a mistyped priority or
+a tag with a space could all end up stored. The list needed to reject these at the one place every
+screen goes through: `add`, `rename` and `tag`. `r4-errors-as-result` forbids `src/domain/` from
+throwing, so rejection has to be a `Result`, like every other failure the list reports.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `TodoErrorCode` (`src/domain/result.ts`) gained a fourth value, `'invalid-input'`, kept separate
+  from `'invalid-state'`: `'invalid-state'` is about a task's status (e.g. completing an already-done
+  task), `'invalid-input'` is about the shape of the data itself, regardless of any task's state.
+- Three small, single-purpose validators live in `src/domain/task.ts`, next to the functions that
+  shape a task, each returning `Result<T>`: `validateTitle` (trims, rejects empty-after-trim or over
+  `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH` (120) characters, returns the trimmed title), `validatePriority` (passes
+  `undefined` through, rejects anything not in `PRIORITIES`), and `validateTag` (rejects empty or
+  containing whitespace). Each error message says which rule failed.
+- `TaskList.add/rename/tag` (`src/domain/list.ts`) run the relevant validator(s) first, before any
+  lookup or the existing duplicate-title check, and return the validator's own error result
+  unchanged on failure. Validating before mutating anything means a rejected input is a pure no-op:
+  nothing in the list changes, as required.
+- `untag` is deliberately left unvalidated: a tag that fails `validateTag` could never have been
+  stored by `tag` in the first place, so untagging it is already a harmless no-op via the existing
+  "removing a tag it doesn't have changes nothing" behaviour.
+- Priority is only validated in `add`, since there is no method to change a task's priority after
+  creation.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- No existing `TaskList` or `NewTask` type signature changed, so this is purely additive for callers
+  that already provide valid input; callers that were sending invalid input through now get
+  `{ ok: false, error: { code: 'invalid-input', message } }` instead of having it silently stored.
+- A rename to a title that is both invalid and would collide with an existing task reports the
+  validation error, not the duplicate error: validation runs first, since it doesn't depend on
+  looking any task up.
+- `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH` is exported from `task.ts` (not re-exported from `src/index.ts`) as the one
+  place the limit is defined, should a screen want to mirror it in a form's `maxlength`.
