@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+---
+id: task-003-validate-title-priority-and-tag-input-on-add-rename-and-tag
+type: task
+title: "Validate title, priority and tag input on add, rename and tag"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, and odd tasks show up. Reject invalid
+input with a clear error that says what is wrong:
+
+- a title that is empty, or only spaces;
+- a title longer than 120 characters;
+- a priority other than `low`, `normal` and `high`;
+- a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+This applies when a task is added, renamed or tagged. When input is rejected, nothing in the list
+changes.
+
+## What I did
+
+- `src/domain/result.ts`: added `'invalid-input'` to `TodoErrorCode`, the code for every validation
+  failure below (distinct from `'invalid-state'`, which is about a task's status, not its input).
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: added three validating functions, each returning a `Result` per
+  `r4-errors-as-result` rather than throwing, with a message that says what is wrong:
+  - `validateTitle(title)`: trims, then rejects an empty (or only-spaces) result, and a trimmed
+    result longer than the new `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH` (120) constant; returns the trimmed title.
+  - `validatePriority(priority)`: passes `undefined` through (priority is optional); rejects anything
+    not in `PRIORITIES`.
+  - `validateTag(tag)`: rejects an empty string, or one containing any whitespace character.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: wired the three validators into the `TaskList` methods that take the
+  corresponding input, before any other check or mutation, so a rejected input leaves the list
+  untouched:
+  - `add`: validates `input.title`, then `input.priority`, then every tag in `input.tags` (in that
+    order, returning on the first failure) before the existing duplicate-title check.
+  - `rename`: validates `newTitle` before looking up the task or checking for a duplicate title.
+  - `tag`: validates `tag` before looking up the task.
+  - `untag` is unchanged: removing a tag that could never have been added (because it would have
+    failed `validateTag`) is a harmless no-op, not a case that needs rejecting.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: added tests for each rule on `add` (including the 120-character boundary as a
+  happy-path case), for the title rules on `rename`, and for the tag rules on `tag`; each rejection
+  test also asserts the list (or the task's title/tags/`updatedAt`) is unchanged.
+
+Wrote the new assertions first and watched them fail (7 red) against the old implementation, then
+implemented the above (21/21 green).
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+None: the existing `TaskList`/`NewTask` method signatures are unchanged, so no caller outside this
+package needs updating. Callers that were relying on invalid input silently passing through (e.g. a
+screen that stored a priority of `'urgent'` as typed, or an empty or spaced tag) now get a `Result`
+with `error.code === 'invalid-input'` instead, and the invalid value is not stored.
